{"id": "post-15307-77d6fc1f", "body": "\nMilton,\n\nKaczynski wrote:\n\n���Presumably a true-believing nazi, for instance, is very \ndifferent psychologically from a true-believing leftist. \n Because of their capacity  for single-minded devotion \nto a cause, True Believers are a useful, perhaps a \nnecessary, ingredient of any revolutionary movement.���   \n\tIndustrial Society And Its Future, by ���FC��� (para. 222).\n\n���[N]ot all activist movements are leftist, and some \nactivist movements (e.g., radical environmentalism) \nseem to include both personalities of the leftist type \nand personalities of thoroughly un-leftist types who \nought to know better than to collaborate with leftists.���\n\tIndustrial Society And Its Future, by ���FC���  (para. 227)    \n\nWould you agree with me that Kaczynski wants the \nsupport of the Nazis?  And absolutely does *not*\nwant the support of any leftists?  For example, \namong EF! members, he only wants those who are\n\"thoroughly unleftist\" (of which there definitely are \nsome).\n\nThe National Alliance supporter is regularly posting\nthe manifesto on the various newsgroups.  So would\nyou agree with me that some Nazis support Kaczynski?\n\n(And would you agree that it is a representative of the\nNational Alliance who is publicly supporting Kaczynski\nby constantly publishing the manifesto?\nAs you did when you promoted the National Alliance.\n\nWould the fellow posting it be posting it if Dr. Pierce\n objected?\n\nHave you read Pierce's 1972 \"Man and Technology\" essay so\nas to know Pierce's views on technology and the environment? \n\nTo the same effect, Dannie Hawkins cogently argued:  \n\n���It seems ���Unabomber��� has a very good understanding of \not only leftists, but weak ass conservatives too, which \nwould overlap to include many weak ass rightists as well.  \nI believe [he] has a much deeper understanding of our \nTrue human natures than the vast majority of people, \nand [that] understanding, along with his far-sightedness,  \nlead him to write his/F.C.'s  manifesto.  \n\t\tDannie Hawkins\n\t\tof W.A.R. [White Aryan Resistance]\n\t\tin alt.politics.greens��� \n\nSimilarly, the October 1995 W.A.R. newsletter opined:\n\n\n���The Unabomber -- A Volkisch Philosopher?���\t\n\tThe F.C. suggests they represent a kind of anarchism, but clearly not the\n syndicalists sort that has occurred when ���anarchists��� have taken power in the\n past.  In reality, \nthe represent ���volkism,��� or the pursuit of Gemeinschaft.  \nIn doing so, they go as far as the volkisch of Hitler���s world \nview, but oppose the formation of entire states built on the philosophy...���\n\nSo would you agree that one of the leading Nazi groups\nfeel that Kaczynski qua Unabomber reprsents \"volkism\",\nor the pursuit of Gemeinschaft.\n\nI never said that Kaczynski wrote or telephoned \nany Nazi group.   To say that one would have to know \nthe detail of what was found in Kaczynski's cabin.\n\nAnd, by the way, not that it is particularly germane\nto Kaczynski's brand of technophobe anarchism, but since\nyou brought it up, I should note that Kaczynski has\nargued that Mexicans are not non-White.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "matches": [{"start": 59, "end": 120, "paragraph": 222, "unit": "p222", "location": "body"}, {"start": 136, "end": 305, "paragraph": 222, "unit": "p222", "location": "body"}, {"start": 384, "end": 647, "paragraph": 227, "unit": "p227", "location": "body"}], "headers": {"From": "ross253212@aol.com", "Date": "1997/11/08", "Subject": "More Questions for Milton", "Message-ID": "<19971108032100.WAA18603@ladder02.news.aol.com>", "Newsgroups": "alt.fan.unabomber", "References": "", "In-Reply-To": "", "Organization": "AOL http://www.aol.com"}, "category": "quotation_in_post"}